{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Who forms…</b> He stated a thing and its opposite." "<b>And creates darkness.</b> From the root of בריאה in the sense of גזירה, for darkness is nothing but the absence of light." "<b>And creates evil.</b> Like it; and behold, evil is war, the opposite of peace, or disease in the body of a human being, which fights against the nature. And he mentioned this in this passage, namely that He will strengthen Cyrus against the king of Babylon."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:09.550138541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}